  "structural_change": "serial-pub-fb0d25867 GRT-0116 (247 edges at 36% usage) concentrated at x 20-40 / y 80-160 = the W channel between the die W face and the 64x512 SRAM (x 23.3, 86.4-164.2) plus its SE corner. Cut arithmetic from the routed ODB: W face 2,082 pins (9.6/um), ~760 of them on y 86-164 facing the macro, which blocks M2-M4, so they must turn vertical in the 23.3 um channel together with the macro's 792 W-side signal pins: ~776 nets cross a horizontal cut at mid-macro vs 23.3 um x 34.8 tr/um = 811 tracks (0.96 > 0.60). Re-shape: SRAM to x 44.928 (W channel 44.9 um: 776/1563 = 0.50), CF SRAMs to 259.2 keeping the 43 um E channel, outline 345.6 -> 367.2 x 216 (+6.25%); same RTL, pins, benches.",
